# Personal Data Protection (GitHub Commits)

This repository must never expose personal identity. Treat this as a hard security requirement.

## Commit identity (mandatory)

When creating any git commit in this repo:

- **Author name** must be the GitHub handle only: `BeanCounter11`
- **Author email** must be the GitHub noreply address: `BeanCounter11@users.noreply.github.com`
- Prefer one-shot flags (do **not** set global `user.name` / `user.email` to personal data):

```bash
git -c user.name="BeanCounter11" -c user.email="BeanCounter11@users.noreply.github.com" commit -m "..."
```

- Same identity for **committer** (the `-c` flags above cover both when used for `git commit`).

## File contents (mandatory)

Never write into tracked files:

- Personal / legal names
- Personal email addresses (any `@` mailbox that is not a GitHub `users.noreply.github.com` address)
- Phone numbers, home addresses, or other PII

Use the GitHub handle or project brand (`buildforjoy.dev`) for copyright, credits, and contact wording.

## Before push

- Confirm staged diffs and commit metadata contain no personal name/email.
- Do not force-push rewritten history unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Leave local-only paths (e.g. `.cursor/` agent caches) untracked unless the user asks to commit them.

## If personal data is found

Stop. Remove it from files and/or rewrite the commit identity before pushing. Do not push and “fix later.”
